      "dom_id": "question-33800",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Calculate the diameter of a sphere given that its volume is $972\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We can find the volume of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nV=\\frac{4}{3}\\pi \\cdot {r}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting $V=972\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{3}$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {r}^{3} \\\\ 972\\pi  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {r}^{3} \\\\ 972\\pi \\cdot \\frac{3}{4\\pi } & ={r}^{3} \\\\ {r}^{3} & =729.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nr=\\sqrt[3]{729}=9\\,\\text{m}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the diameter of the sphere is\n\n$$\nd=2r=2\\cdot 9=18\\,\\text{m}.\n$$",
